{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "composite": false,
    "declaration": false,
    "declarationMap": false,
    "noEmit": true,
    "incremental": true,
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  /**
   * The solution root does two jobs. It builds the emitting package projects
   * through `references`, and it is itself the non-emitting project that
   * type-checks everything outside a package's `rootDir`: the root Vitest
   * config and every package test suite.
   *
   * Tests are checked here rather than from a per-package `tsconfig.test.json`
   * because a referenced project may not disable emit (TS6310), so a test
   * project could only join `tsc -b` by emitting `.js`/`.d.ts` for test files
   * into a throwaway directory. Checking them from the root instead keeps
   * `rootDir: src` and `dist/` free of test output, adds no build artefacts,
   * and still means a plain `tsc -b` — and therefore `npm run check` — fails on
   * a type error in a test.
   *
   * Tests import `@kept/core`, never `packages/kept-core/src/**` — the barrel
   * is the only consumer entry point (design §2.1). The compiler tolerates a
   * deep import here because a project reference redirects it to the built
   * declaration, so that rule is upheld by review and, later, by the
   * source-scan tests, not by this file.
   *
   * The Ledger's non-browser half joins the same job for the same reason. A Next
   * application is `noEmit`, so `apps/ledger` cannot be a project reference
   * either (TS6310 again), and `apps/ledger/tsconfig.json` is deliberately not
   * listed above. Naming its `lib/` and `test/` trees here instead means a type
   * error in the design tokens or in a source scan fails a plain `tsc -b`, and
   * therefore `npm run check`, from the first commit — and it checks them under
   * this project's `lib: ["ES2022"]` with no DOM, which is the stronger claim:
   * the token mirror and the scans have no business touching the DOM. The
   * browser-facing half — `app/**`, `components/**` and their JSX — is checked by
   * `tsc -p apps/ledger --noEmit`, which is where `jsx` and the DOM libs live.
   */
  "include": [
    "vitest.config.ts",
    "packages/*/test/**/*.ts",
    "apps/ledger/lib/**/*.ts",
    "apps/ledger/test/**/*.ts"
  ],
  "references": [
    { "path": "packages/kept-core" },
    { "path": "packages/kept-cli" }
  ]
}
